 36MG c  2016Do03: measurement of B(E2) and deformation lengths for the first   
 36MG2c  2+ state by Coulomb excitation and nuclear inelastic scattering,       
 36MG3c  respectively. Beam={+36}Mg at 223 MeV/nucleon for lead target and 218  
 36MG4c  MeV/nucleon for carbon target produced at RIBF-RIKEN in                
 36MG5c  {+9}Be({+48}Ca,X),E=345 MeV/nucleon primary reaction, followed by      
 36MG6c  separation of ions of interest using BigRIPS fragment separator and    
 36MG7c  ZeroDegree spectrometer for the analysis of events in terms of atomic  
 36MG8c  number (Z) and mass-to-charge (A/Q) ratio based on B|r-|DE-tof         
 36MG9c  method. Beam purity was |?16%. The gamma rays were detected by DALI2   
 36MGac  array of 186 NaI(Tl) scintillation detectors covering angles of 18|'   
 36MGbc  to 146|'. Measured E|g, I|g, {+36}Mg-|g-coin, cross section. Deduced   
 36MGcc  B(E2) from data for Pb target (dominated by Coulomb excitation) and    
 36MGdc  deformation length from data for carbon target (dominated by nuclear   
 36MGec  inelastic scattering) by comparing the measured cross sections to      
 36MGfc  those calculated by ECIS97 coupled-channel code using the rotational   
 36MGgc  model. Comparison with shell-model calculations                        
